USB CCTV Recorder package notes
===============================

The package installs the frozen application below /usr/lib/usb-cctv-recorder,
its launcher in /usr/bin, a KDE desktop entry, hicolor icons, and the static
systemd user unit below /usr/lib/systemd/user. The worker is never enabled at
login. It starts only when the GUI requests it.

On installation or upgrade, the package reloads the invoking user's systemd
manager when that session can be identified. The application reloads that user
manager again immediately before it starts the worker, so graphical installers
that do not provide SUDO_USER are handled safely as well.

Uninstalling this package does not remove user data. The following paths remain
until the user deliberately removes them:

* Configuration: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/usb-cctv-recorder/ (normally
  ~/.config/usb-cctv-recorder/)
* Derived SQLite catalogue and state: $XDG_STATE_HOME/usb-cctv-recorder/
  (normally ~/.local/state/usb-cctv-recorder/)
* Cache: $XDG_CACHE_HOME/usb-cctv-recorder/ (normally ~/.cache/usb-cctv-recorder/)
* Recordings: ~/Videos/USB-CCTV-Recorder/ by default, or the media root selected
  by the user.

Before an upgrade or removal, stop an active recording safely. Package upgrades
do not replace or migrate media. Existing private configuration is read through
the application migration path, and the catalogue can be rebuilt from media and
manifests with `usb-cctv-recorder --rebuild-catalogue --media-root <absolute path>`.
